/**
 * Article body chunker with overlap.
 *
 * Splits long text into overlapping chunks suitable for independent embedding.
 * Chunk-based retrieval beats whole-document embedding in practice:
 *   - A 4000-char article has one averaged representation; important details wash out.
 *   - A 4000-char article split into 8 × 600-char chunks surfaces specific passages.
 *
 * We use character-based sizing (not token-based) because:
 *   - No tokenizer dependency at ingestion time.
 *   - Gemini's embedding model accepts up to ~2048 tokens; 2000 chars is well within that.
